README (patch ignores everything above the first "---" line)
=====================================================================
amara-voice-dictate.diff: one on-device dictation on request, for Amara OS (Lane W4, 2026-11-14)

Why: voice adds and check-ins need text from the mic, on this Mac only. Amara Voice already owns the mic
stream and has Whisper base.en (asr.py, used by main() as `asr`), but nothing records+transcribes ONCE on
request: the only inbound signals are SIGUSR1 (stop speaking) and, with amara-voice-speak.diff, speak/request.json.
Amara OS cannot open the mic itself without a second stream fighting the loop's.

What it adds (amara_voice.py only, ~90 lines, stdlib, no new package, no network, no cloud):
  - dictate_watcher thread: polls <amara-voice>/dictate/request.json every 0.4 s, reads and deletes it.
    Request: {"id","purpose":"add"|"checkin","max_secs","ts"}. Queued only if ts is within 15 s, purpose is
    known and none is already pending (fail closed; anything else is dropped).
  - The MAIN loop (sole owner of the mic stream) answers it while idle: Ears.next_utterance(interruptible=True)
    returns early only before anyone starts speaking. It chimes, records ONE utterance (max_secs, 3..30), runs the
    local Whisper, and writes dictate/result.json = {"id","ok","text"} (tmp + rename). Text only, capped at 500 chars.
  - The audio exists only in memory: `del audio` right after transcription; nothing is written to disk. Not sent to
    Hermes, not logged, not a wake turn. Skipped (ok=false) while an alarm/reminder is ringing.
  - Writes its pid to logs/dictate_ready at start and removes it at exit. Amara OS treats dictation as READY only
    when that pid is the running amara_voice.py; otherwise the mic buttons stay disabled.
  - No navy gate: dictation is always on-device (local Whisper, text-only result), so it works in normal use.

Compatibility with amara-voice-speak.diff: independent. Made against the unpatched file; the hunks are separate
and it uses a local `import atexit`, so the two apply in either order (checked with patch --dry-run on temp copies).

What Taisun applies (live, non-git dir):
  1. cd ~/projects/amara-voice && cp amara_voice.py amara_voice.py.bak-$(date +%F)
  2. patch -p1 --dry-run < ~/projects/nexus-amara/tasks/proposed/amara-voice-dictate.diff   (check it applies)
  3. patch -p1 < ~/projects/nexus-amara/tasks/proposed/amara-voice-dictate.diff
  4. Restart Amara Voice (Voice panel: Stop, Start, or ./amara stop && ./amara start).
  5. First use: macOS may ask for microphone access for the Python the loop runs under (it already has it if the
     loop hears you today). Never type or dictate into the app while testing unless it is you.

How to test (local only):
  1. ls ~/projects/amara-voice/logs/dictate_ready -> loop pid; ls -ld dictate/ -> 0700.
  2. Open Life > New goal; the mic button is now enabled (disabled before). No Navy switch is needed.
  3. Click the mic, say "run three times a week". The text appears in the box and goes to the usual
     "Check before saving" preview; nothing is saved until you press Save.
  4. Home > Check-in mic: same, text fills the box; you still press Save.
  5. find ~/projects/amara-voice -newer logs/dictate_ready -name '*.wav' -o -newer logs/dictate_ready -name '*.npy'
     -> nothing; ls dictate/ -> empty between uses.
  6. Stop Amara Voice: logs/dictate_ready disappears and the mic buttons disable again.
